@payment_social_capacity
title: Open transparent calls for housing, care and local transport
subtitle: Spends two released tranches on local capacity Lewica can point at.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_first_payment_paid = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 5;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
Q.government_delivery += 4;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Open calls turn the first transfer into visible local capacity.";
Q.news_headline = "The first KPO calls fund care, housing and local links";
!}

The calls go out unrestricted: any municipality with a site and a signature
can bid, and the scoring sheet is published with them. Housing associations,
care providers and two dozen transport authorities discover they are allowed to
want something.

The ministries dislike open competition because it produces winners they did
not choose. That is the point. Within a year there will be work in counties
that have never once been the beneficiary of a national programme.

- @kpo_result: Open the first calls

