        "The PiS cabinet remains under Article 7 and receives no payment or delivery credit.";
    Q.news_headline =
        "Article 7 and the recovery-fund file remain stalled under PiS";
}
!}

= May 2024 — Europe judges the legal record

[? if kpo_article7_reward: Europe closes the Article 7 procedure after the
action plan and first payment. That is a diplomatic and fiscal reward, not a
certificate that every Polish court, prosecutor and appointment is settled.?]
[? if not kpo_article7_reward: The surviving PiS cabinet has supplied neither
the political change nor the legal milestones required for closure. Article 7
stays open and the first payment remains unavailable; Lewica can document the
failure, but cannot manufacture European approval from opposition.?]

[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_public_credit >= 5: The Left already has a
recognisable KPO claim. Partners now want the scoreboard blurred.?]
[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_public_credit < 5: The government has the
European headline; the Left still needs to connect it to something people
use.?]

