on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kpo_milestones += 3;
Q.kpo_delivery += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The correction is not glamorous, but it keeps a weak file financeable.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition funds a KPO correction before the budget vote";
!}

A small team of civil servants and outside auditors goes through the weak
annexes before the tranche is promised to anything. They find what such teams
find: optimistic timetables, double-counted co-financing and two schemes that
cannot legally start.

Nobody will ever cheer for this. It is also the difference between a budget
built on money that will arrive and one built on money that a Commission desk
officer is about to send back.

- @kpo_result: Fund the correction team

@budget_gate_paper
title: Count legal adoption as delivery and protect the ordinary budget
subtitle: Improve the spreadsheet now and pass implementation risk into next year.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 4;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 2;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 4;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 2;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 6;
Q.labor_credibility -= 3;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The spreadsheet improves while implementation and later-payment risk worsen.";
Q.news_headline = "The budget counts KPO statutes before institutions can deliver them";
!}

Legal adoption is entered as delivery, the spreadsheet balances and the
ordinary budget survives December without a public argument. Every one of those
statements is technically true.

The implementation the adoption was supposed to trigger has not begun. We have
moved the problem into next year, where it will be larger, and where the people
now defending the figures may not be the people who have to answer for them.

- @kpo_result: Count the adoption

@budget_gate_opposition
title: Separate KPO grants from the government's unfunded promises
subtitle: Expose double counting without pretending the opposition controls state spending.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The shadow budget exposes double counting without taking responsibility for state spending.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left marks every KPO grant in the opposition budget ledger";
!}

We take the government's budget apart on one point: which promises are funded
from European grants and which are being counted twice. It requires no cabinet
authority, only the patience to reconcile two documents the government prefers
to present separately.

Ministers dislike it because the answer is embarrassing and difficult to
dispute. It also commits us to nothing — we have exposed the arithmetic without
having to say which of the double-counted promises we would drop.

- @kpo_result: Publish the separation


@kpo_midterm_review_2025
# prose-audit: Grade A — The review turns on whether money follows readiness or ownership, and every route now has a loser on the page: ministries raided for reallocation, a deliberately boring protocol with close dates, a good slogan attached to projects nobody re-costed.
title: The KPO midterm review
subtitle: Delivery competes with coalition self-preservation.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 20
order: 30
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 10
on-arrival: {!
const kpoMidNum = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
Q.kpo_delivery = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_delivery, 0);
Q.kpo_milestones = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_milestones, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_available = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_funds_available, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_spent = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_funds_spent, 0);
Q.kpo_public_credit = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_public_credit, 0);
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure, 8) + 4;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_delayed = kpoMidNum(Q.kpo_funds_delayed, 0);
const kpoMidRestraint = kpoMidNum(Q.government_procedural_restraint, 45);
const kpoMidDualism = kpoMidNum(Q.legal_dualism, 50);
const kpoMidScore =
    Q.kpo_milestones * 2 + Q.kpo_delivery * 2 +
    kpoMidRestraint * 0.15 - kpoMidDualism * 0.12 -
    Q.kpo_shortcut_debt * 2 - Q.kpo_deadline_pressure;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
if (kpoMidScore >= 18) {
    Q.kpo_midterm_status = "Additional payment cleared";
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Payments flowing; completion monitored";
    Q.kpo_funds_available += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "A further payment clears, leaving a political fight over delivery.";
    Q.news_headline = "The KPO review clears another payment";
} else if (kpoMidScore >= 2) {
    Q.kpo_midterm_status = "Payment conditional on a correction file";
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Correction period";
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 2;
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "Money remains available only if the coalition repairs a thin implementation file.";
    Q.news_headline = "The KPO review demands a correction file";
} else {
    Q.kpo_midterm_status = "Payment delayed";
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Payment delayed; milestones and legality disputed";
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 3;
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 7;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "A delayed payment turns technical debt into a coalition crisis.";
    Q.news_headline = "A KPO payment is delayed as deadlines close in";
}
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
!}

