One slogan, one Chancellery, one promise that every project will be finished.
It is a good line and it travels well, which is the strongest argument for it.

It is also a promise made about projects nobody has re-costed. **[+
prime_minister +]** now owns each of them individually, and so does every party
that stood behind the podium while the promise was made.

- @kpo_result: Centralise the rescue

@midterm_opposition_support
title: Support a narrow corrective act for labour and local projects
subtitle: Supply votes for a narrow repair while leaving implementation with the cabinet.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
