= December 2025 — Fund completion or hide the delay

Available but uncommitted: **[+ kpo_uncommitted +]** blocks. Deadline pressure:
**[+ kpo_deadline_pressure +]**.

- @bridge_enforcement
- @bridge_reserve
- @bridge_defer
- @bridge_opposition

@bridge_enforcement
title: Fund inspectors, permitting teams and local co-financing
subtitle: Spends two released tranches on the staff who turn approvals into contracts.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The unlocked reserve is already committed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 2;
Q.budget += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 5;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Administrative capacity turns European money into usable budget room.";
Q.news_headline = "The budget funds the people required to finish KPO projects";
!}

The money goes on inspectors, permitting officers and the local co-financing
desks that turn an approved project into a signed contract. It is the least
photogenic possible use of a European recovery fund.

It is also the binding constraint. Half the delay in this programme has been
municipalities without a person qualified to complete the paperwork, and that
is a problem money can actually solve.

- @kpo_result: Fund the staff

@bridge_reserve
title: Keep a smaller corrective reserve behind the budget
subtitle: Protect a smaller fiscal reserve and leave much of the completion risk unresolved.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget += 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, Q.fiscal_stress - 1);
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The reserve protects fiscal room, but cannot finish many projects by itself.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition keeps a KPO correction reserve";
!}

A smaller reserve is held back to protect the budget, which it will do. The
completion risk it does not cover is simply left where it is.

We have chosen fiscal safety over finishing the work, and done so knowingly.
When projects fail to complete next year, the reserve will be what prevented
that failure from also becoming a budget crisis. It will not have prevented the
failure.

- @kpo_result: Keep the reserve

@bridge_defer
title: Protect the headline budget and push implementation into 2026
subtitle: Preserve the headline budget and send the unfinished work into the final year.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 6;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 3;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 5;
Q.labor_credibility -= 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The ordinary budget looks safer and the recovery deadline becomes harsher.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition defers KPO implementation into its final year";
!}

The ordinary budget comes through December looking sound. The unfinished work
goes into 2026, which is the last year available and therefore the year in
which nothing can be deferred again.

Everyone in the room understands the trade. The people who will have to
administer it are mostly not in the room.

- @kpo_result: Protect the headline

@bridge_opposition
title: Make KPO absorption a condition for any budget favour
subtitle: Make absorption the price of our cooperation without claiming cabinet authority.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The opposition converts a technical deadline into a visible condition for cooperation.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left ties every budget favour to KPO absorption";
!}

We make absorption the price: no cooperation on the budget until the
government can show what proportion of the fund has actually been drawn down
and spent. It converts a technical measure into a political test.

The government can refuse. It cannot refuse quietly, because the figure is
published quarterly by the Commission and anyone can look it up.

- @kpo_result: Set the condition


@kpo_pip_milestone_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The strongest chain here: vote, signature and enforcement stay distinct, and the aftermaths carry that distinction into labour courts taking the load, a specialist team with an expiry date, and a milestone that is legible in Brussels and hollow at the workplace.
title: The PIP milestone reaches its legal test
subtitle: Passage, presidential action and enforcement are three different hurdles.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 4 and labor_reform_settled = 0
call: poland_senate.refresh
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
    ? Number(Q.kpo_milestones) : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery)) ? Number(Q.kpo_delivery) : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_available)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure)
        : 10;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt)
        : 0;
const pipSejmTotal = Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460;
const pipRecordedGovernmentSupport = Number(Q.government_support_seats);
const pipCoalitionWithoutLeft = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0) -
        (Q.left_in_government
            ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats) || 0)
            : 0)
);
const pipGovernmentBaseVotes =
    Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
        ? (
            Number.isFinite(pipRecordedGovernmentSupport)
                ? Math.max(0, pipRecordedGovernmentSupport)
                : pipCoalitionWithoutLeft
        )
        : 0;
Q.pip_coalition_defections = Math.min(
    pipGovernmentBaseVotes,
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(
            ((Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 30) / 7
        )
    )
);
const pipGovernmentVotes = Math.max(
    0,
    pipGovernmentBaseVotes - Q.pip_coalition_defections
);
const pipLeftVotes = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || Number(Q.left_seats) || 0
);
Q.pip_sejm_yes = Math.min(
    pipSejmTotal,
    Math.round(pipGovernmentVotes + pipLeftVotes)
);
const pipOppositionPool = Math.max(0, pipSejmTotal - Q.pip_sejm_yes);
Q.pip_sejm_absent = Math.min(
    pipOppositionPool,
    Math.max(8, Math.round(pipSejmTotal * 0.02))
);
Q.pip_sejm_abstain = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, pipOppositionPool - Q.pip_sejm_absent),
    Math.round(pipOppositionPool * 0.06)
);
Q.pip_sejm_no = Math.max(
    0,
    pipSejmTotal - Q.pip_sejm_yes -
        Q.pip_sejm_absent - Q.pip_sejm_abstain
);
Q.pip_sejm_present =
    Q.pip_sejm_yes + Q.pip_sejm_no + Q.pip_sejm_abstain;
Q.pip_sejm_quorum = Math.ceil(pipSejmTotal / 2);
Q.pip_sejm_threshold = Q.pip_sejm_no + 1;
Q.pip_sejm_passed =
    Q.pip_sejm_present >= Q.pip_sejm_quorum &&
    Q.pip_sejm_yes > Q.pip_sejm_no ? 1 : 0;
const pipSenateTotal = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(Number(Q.senate_total) || 100)
);
const pipSenateThreshold = Math.floor(pipSenateTotal / 2) + 1;
// The scene's `call:` refresh completes after this arrival block, so calculate
// cabinet membership from live party/portfolio state rather than stale cache.
const pipCabinetSenators = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        pipSenateTotal,
        (Q.government_party == "pis"
            ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_pis_seats) || 0) : 0) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "ko" || Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_ko_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "p2050" || Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_p2050_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "psl" || Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_psl_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "lewica" || Q.left_in_government
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0) : 0
        )
    )
);
const pipLeftSenators = Q.left_in_government
    ? 0
    : Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0));
const pipIndependentSenators = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.senate_independent_seats) || 0)
);
const pipIndependentSupport = Math.round(
    pipIndependentSenators *
        Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) / 100
);
Q.pip_senate_yes = Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? Math.min(
        pipSenateTotal,
        pipCabinetSenators + pipLeftSenators + pipIndependentSupport
    )
    : 0;
Q.pip_senate_no = Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? Math.max(0, pipSenateTotal - Q.pip_senate_yes)
    : 0;
Q.pip_senate_threshold = pipSenateThreshold;
Q.pip_senate_action = !Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? "No Senate review"
    : (
        Q.pip_senate_yes < pipSenateThreshold
            ? "Senate rejected the bill"
            : (
                pipCabinetSenators >= pipSenateThreshold
                    ? "Senate accepted the bill without amendment"
                    : "Senate adopted a worker-appeals amendment"
            )
    );
Q.pip_senate_return_yes = 0;
Q.pip_senate_return_threshold = 0;
Q.pip_senate_return_passed = 0;
let pipParliamentPassed = Boolean(Q.pip_sejm_passed);
if (
    Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the bill" ||
    Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate adopted a worker-appeals amendment"
) {
    Q.pip_senate_return_yes = Q.pip_sejm_yes;
    Q.pip_senate_return_threshold =
        Math.floor(Q.pip_sejm_present / 2) + 1;
    Q.pip_senate_return_passed =
        Q.pip_senate_return_yes >= Q.pip_senate_return_threshold ? 1 : 0;
    if (Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the bill") {
        pipParliamentPassed = Boolean(Q.pip_senate_return_passed);
    }
}
Q.pip_parliament_passed = pipParliamentPassed ? 1 : 0;
const pipRightWingPresident = [
    "Andrzej Duda",
    String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
    "Sławomir Mentzen",
    "Grzegorz Braun"
].includes(Q.president_name);
const pipHostilePresident =
    (
        pipRightWingPresident ||
        (
            Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
            Q.president_name == Q.pres_2025_winner
        )
    ) &&
    Q.government_party != "pis";
const pipVeto =
    Q.pip_parliament_passed &&
    pipHostilePresident &&
    (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) < 45;
Q.pip_law_enacted = Q.pip_parliament_passed && !pipVeto ? 1 : 0;
Q.pip_presidential_action = !Q.pip_parliament_passed
    ? "No bill reached the President"
    : (pipVeto ? "Presidential veto" : "Signed into law");
if (Q.pip_law_enacted) {
    Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The enacted inspection reform records a legal milestone; enforcement remains open.";
    Q.news_headline =
        "The PIP reform passes, is signed and moves to enforcement";
} else if (pipVeto) {
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "A presidential veto blocks the legal milestone before implementation.";
    Q.news_headline = "The President vetoes the PIP milestone bill";
} else {
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        Q.pip_sejm_passed
            ? "The Senate procedure stops the PIP bill before presidential action."
            : "The PIP bill lacks a Sejm majority and records no milestone.";
    Q.news_headline = Q.pip_sejm_passed
        ? "The PIP milestone bill fails during Senate review"
        : "The PIP milestone bill fails in the Sejm";
}
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
!}

= April 2026 — A milestone at the workplace

[? if pip_law_enacted: The law gives the State Labour Inspection stronger
tools against civil contracts that conceal employment. The European legal
milestone is easier to record than thousands of inspections, appeals and
converted contracts.?]
[? if not pip_law_enacted: The proposal receives **[+ pip_sejm_yes +] yes**
against **[+ pip_sejm_no +] no**, with **[+ pip_sejm_abstain +] abstentions**
and **[+ pip_sejm_absent +] absent**. It needs **[+ pip_sejm_threshold +] yes**
among votes cast and a quorum of **[+ pip_sejm_quorum +]**.?]
Senate: **[+ pip_senate_action +]** (**[+ pip_senate_yes +]–[+
pip_senate_no +]**). [? if pip_senate_return_threshold > 0: The Sejm return
vote records **[+ pip_senate_return_yes +] yes** against an absolute-majority
threshold of **[+ pip_senate_return_threshold +]**.?] Presidential result:
**[+ pip_presidential_action +]**. No KPO legal milestone or inspector power
exists until the full parliamentary procedure and signature are complete.
[? if pip_coalition_defections > 0: Coalition dissent removes
**[+ pip_coalition_defections +] expected government votes**; those MPs are
not recast as conveniently absent opposition members.?]

- @pip_full_enforcement
- @pip_kpo_team
- @pip_paper
- @pip_opposition
- @pip_revise_bill
- @pip_opposition_campaign

@pip_full_enforcement
title: Fund inspectors, appeal capacity and worker legal aid
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The government budget has no room for recurring enforcement.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 6;
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 4);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.labor_credibility += 6;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.court_backlog += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 6;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The milestone becomes workplace power, with a manageable new burden on courts.";
Q.news_headline = "Inspectors receive the staff to enforce the KPO labour reform";
!}

Inspectors, appeal capacity and legal aid for workers are funded together,
because an inspectorate without an appeals route produces findings and not
outcomes. Employers who have been reclassifying staff for a decade start
receiving visits.

The labour courts take the load. They were already slow, and this makes them
slower — the difference is that the cases now arriving are ones that would
previously never have been brought at all.

- @kpo_result: Fund the inspectorate

@pip_kpo_team
title: Use the remaining KPO block for a specialist enforcement team
subtitle: Spends one released tranche on early enforcement before national capacity exists.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No unlocked recovery block remains.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 4;
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.court_backlog += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A specialist team produces credible early enforcement without full national capacity.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO technical money launches the PIP enforcement team";
!}

A specialist unit is stood up on the remaining European money: small, well
paid, and pointed at the sectors where reclassification is most systematic.
It will produce real cases within months.

It is not a national capability and nobody should call it one. When the
European money ends, this team ends with it unless the domestic budget adopts
them — which is next year's argument, prepared today.

- @kpo_result: Build the team

@pip_paper
title: Issue guidance, record the milestone and postpone staffing
subtitle: Give Brussels a legible milestone and workers an inspectorate without staff.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 4;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 3;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 5;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 4;
Q.labor_credibility -= 6;
Q.razem_dissent += 8;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The milestone is legible in Brussels and hollow at the workplace.";
Q.news_headline = "The PIP milestone passes without an enforcement budget";
!}

The guidance is issued, the milestone is recorded and Brussels is satisfied.
Legally, the Labour Inspectorate now has powers it did not have last month.

Practically, it has the same number of inspectors it had last month. The
workers the milestone was written for will find that the new power exists and
that nobody has been hired to use it.

- @kpo_result: Record the milestone

@pip_opposition
title: Audit converted contracts, appeals and inspector vacancies
subtitle: Count protected workers and vacancies; the cabinet still has to hire the inspectors.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and pip_law_enacted = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
Q.labor_credibility += 5;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The audit makes implementation, not signature, the measure of the milestone.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left counts workers protected by the PIP reform";
!}

We count the things the government would rather report in aggregate:
contracts actually converted, appeals actually heard, inspector posts actually
filled. Signature is not implementation, and the gap between them is now a
published number.

The cabinet retains every power to close that gap. Our audit simply removes the
option of describing the milestone as complete while the vacancies stand.

- @kpo_result: Publish the audit

@pip_revise_bill
title: Negotiate a narrower bill and return it to Parliament
subtitle: Narrow the bill and return to Parliament without claiming a milestone.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pip_reform_pending = 1;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2);
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
Q.president_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "A narrower PIP bill remains pending; no legal milestone is claimed.";
Q.news_headline =
    "The cabinet reopens the PIP bill instead of claiming a fictional milestone";
!}

The bill goes back to committee stripped of the clauses that lost it the vote.
What returns is genuinely weaker and genuinely passable, and we say so rather
than pretending the retreat is a refinement.

No milestone can be claimed for a bill that has not passed. Unions accept the
narrowing because the alternative on offer is nothing; they also record who
asked them to accept it.

- @kpo_result: Return the narrower bill

@pip_opposition_campaign
title: Publish the failed roll call and organise for a new bill
subtitle: Keep the failed bill alive through workers and the recorded roll call.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and pip_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pip_reform_pending = 1;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "Opposition pressure keeps the bill alive without pretending it passed.";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left publishes the failed PIP vote and organises a new bill";
!}

Every name and every vote goes out, matched to the constituency and to the
workplaces in it where reclassification is common. The bill is dead; the
division list is not.

Organisers now have something specific to campaign on, and several deputies who
expected the vote to vanish into the record discover that it has instead
acquired a local address.

- @kpo_result: Publish the roll call


@kpo_final_window_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — A genuine trilemma at the deadline — finish what can finish, claim less and have it verified, or certify everything and hand the problem to auditors — and each branch now states plainly whose problem it becomes afterwards.
title: The last KPO summer
subtitle: Completion, correction or a frozen final file.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 30
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 7
call: poland_senate.refresh
on-arrival: {!
const kpoFinalNum = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
Q.kpo_delivery = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_delivery, 0);
Q.kpo_milestones = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_milestones, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_available = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_available, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_spent = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_spent, 0);
Q.kpo_public_credit = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_public_credit, 0);
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure, 10) + 4;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_delayed = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_delayed, 0);
Q.pip_final_retry_resolved = 0;
Q.pip_final_retry_status = "No PIP revision was pending";
if (Q.pip_reform_pending) {
    Q.pip_final_retry_resolved = 1;
    if (Q.left_in_government) {
        const pipRetryTotal = Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460;
        const pipRetryNoBefore = Number(Q.pip_sejm_no) || 0;
        const pipRetryShift = Math.min(8, pipRetryNoBefore);
        const pipRetryYes = Math.min(
            pipRetryTotal,
            (Number(Q.pip_sejm_yes) || 0) + pipRetryShift
        );
        const pipRetryNo = Math.max(
            0,
            pipRetryNoBefore - pipRetryShift
        );
        const pipRetryPresent =
            pipRetryYes + pipRetryNo + (Number(Q.pip_sejm_abstain) || 0);
        const pipRetryRightPresident = [
            "Andrzej Duda",
            String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
            "Sławomir Mentzen",
            "Grzegorz Braun"
        ].includes(Q.president_name);
        const pipRetryHostile =
            (
                pipRetryRightPresident ||
                (
                    Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
                    Q.president_name == Q.pres_2025_winner
                )
            ) &&
            Q.government_party != "pis" &&
            (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) < 45;
        const pipRetryPassed =
            pipRetryPresent >= Math.ceil(pipRetryTotal / 2) &&
            pipRetryYes > pipRetryNo;
        Q.pip_sejm_yes = pipRetryYes;
        Q.pip_sejm_no = pipRetryNo;
        Q.pip_sejm_present = pipRetryPresent;
        Q.pip_sejm_quorum = Math.ceil(pipRetryTotal / 2);
        Q.pip_sejm_threshold = pipRetryNo + 1;
        Q.pip_sejm_passed = pipRetryPassed ? 1 : 0;
        const retrySenateTotal = Math.max(
            1,
            Math.round(Number(Q.senate_total) || 100)
        );
        const retrySenateThreshold =
            Math.floor(retrySenateTotal / 2) + 1;
        const retryCabinetSenators = Math.max(
            0,
            Math.min(
                retrySenateTotal,
                (Q.government_party == "pis"
                    ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_pis_seats) || 0) : 0) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "ko" ||
                    Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_ko_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "p2050" ||
                    Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_p2050_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "psl" ||
                    Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_psl_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "lewica" || Q.left_in_government
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0) : 0
                )
            )
        );
        const retryLeftSenators = Q.left_in_government
            ? 0
            : Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0));
        const retryIndependentSupport = Math.round(
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.senate_independent_seats) || 0) *
                Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) /
                100
        );
        Q.pip_senate_yes = pipRetryPassed
            ? Math.min(
                retrySenateTotal,
                retryCabinetSenators + retryLeftSenators +
                    retryIndependentSupport
            )
            : 0;
        Q.pip_senate_no = pipRetryPassed
            ? Math.max(0, retrySenateTotal - Q.pip_senate_yes)
            : 0;
        Q.pip_senate_threshold = retrySenateThreshold;
        Q.pip_senate_action = !pipRetryPassed
            ? "No Senate review"
            : (
                Q.pip_senate_yes < retrySenateThreshold
                    ? "Senate rejected the narrow revision"
                    : (
                        retryCabinetSenators >= retrySenateThreshold
                            ? "Senate accepted the narrow revision"
                            : "Senate amended the narrow revision"
                    )
            );
        Q.pip_senate_return_yes = 0;
        Q.pip_senate_return_threshold = 0;
        Q.pip_senate_return_passed = 0;
        let pipRetryParliamentPassed = Boolean(pipRetryPassed);
        if (
            Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the narrow revision" ||
            Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate amended the narrow revision"
        ) {
            Q.pip_senate_return_yes = pipRetryYes;
            Q.pip_senate_return_threshold =
                Math.floor(pipRetryPresent / 2) + 1;
            Q.pip_senate_return_passed =
                pipRetryYes >= Q.pip_senate_return_threshold ? 1 : 0;
            if (
                Q.pip_senate_action ==
                    "Senate rejected the narrow revision"
            ) {
                pipRetryParliamentPassed =
                    Boolean(Q.pip_senate_return_passed);
            }
        }
        Q.pip_parliament_passed = pipRetryParliamentPassed ? 1 : 0;
        if (pipRetryParliamentPassed && !pipRetryHostile) {
            Q.pip_law_enacted = 1;
            Q.pip_presidential_action = "Narrow revision signed into law";
            Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
            Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2
            );
            Q.pip_final_retry_status =
                "The narrower PIP revision passed and was signed before the final review";
        } else if (pipRetryParliamentPassed) {
            Q.pip_presidential_action = "Narrow revision vetoed";
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
            Q.pip_final_retry_status =
                "The narrower PIP revision passed the Sejm but met another presidential veto";
        } else {
            Q.pip_presidential_action = pipRetryPassed
                ? "Narrow revision stopped in Senate procedure"
                : "Narrow revision failed in the Sejm";
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
            Q.pip_final_retry_status = pipRetryPassed
                ? "The narrower PIP revision passed the Sejm but did not complete Senate procedure"
                : "The narrower PIP revision returned to the Sejm and failed";
        }
    } else {
        Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
        Q.pip_final_retry_status =
            "The opposition PIP bill received no government time before the KPO deadline";
    }
    Q.pip_reform_pending = 0;
}
const kpoFinalRestraint =
    kpoFinalNum(Q.government_procedural_restraint, 45);
const kpoFinalDualism = kpoFinalNum(Q.legal_dualism, 50);
const kpoFinalScore =
    Q.kpo_milestones * 2 + Q.kpo_delivery * 3 +
    Q.kpo_funds_spent * 2 + kpoFinalRestraint * 0.1 -
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - Q.kpo_shortcut_debt * 3 -
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed - kpoFinalDualism * 0.06;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
if (kpoFinalScore >= 70) {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Green — final payment file credible";
    Q.kpo_funds_available += 4;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Final file credible; completion audit pending";
    Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 4;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "A strong delivery record releases the last substantial tranche.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file enters the green lane";
} else if (kpoFinalScore >= 32) {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Amber — corrective completion required";
    Q.kpo_funds_available += 2;
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 1;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Partial release; corrective completion required";
    Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "Part of the final file clears while weak projects enter correction.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file receives a partial green light";
} else {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Red — final payment at risk";
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 4;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Final payment at risk";
    Q.fiscal_stress += 5;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "Missed delivery and shortcut debt threaten the final payment.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file enters a funding crisis";
}
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
!}

= July 2026 — The final deadline

Final status: **[+ kpo_final_status +]**. Uncommitted blocks:
**[+ kpo_uncommitted +]**.

[? if pip_final_retry_resolved: PIP follow-up: **[+ pip_final_retry_status +]**.?]

[? if kpo_final_status = "Green — final payment file credible": Earlier
institutional patience and implementation have created genuine room for a
final delivery choice.?]
[? if kpo_final_status = "Amber — corrective completion required": The file
can still be rescued, but only by abandoning weak projects or accepting a
smaller claim.?]
[? if kpo_final_status = "Red — final payment at risk": The recovery fund is
now a fiscal crisis and a coalition blame game.?]

- @final_ready_work
- @final_independent_audit
- @final_paper_close
- @final_opposition_rescue
- @final_opposition_blame

@final_ready_work
title: Protect ready social projects and abandon prestige schemes
subtitle: Spends up to three released tranches and sacrifices weaker ministerial projects.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: No released tranche remains to redirect.
on-arrival: {!
const finalCommit = Math.min(3, Q.kpo_uncommitted);
Q.kpo_funds_spent += finalCommit;
Q.kpo_delivery += 6;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 4);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.government_delivery += 4;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 6;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The coalition sacrifices prestige projects to finish work people can use.";
Q.news_headline = "The final KPO block moves to projects that can open on time";
!}

Prestige schemes are abandoned so that the projects with a realistic
completion date can be finished properly. Some of the abandoned ones are
handsome, well advanced and belong to ministers who will not forget.

What gets completed is smaller than what was announced in 2022 and it exists.
In the final accounting, a finished clinic outranks a beautifully rendered
proposal, and the people who use it will not know there was ever an argument.

- @kpo_result: Finish what can finish

@final_independent_audit
title: Accept a smaller claim and submit an independent completion audit
subtitle: Lose part of the claim to protect trust in the work that actually finished.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 3;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_shortcut_debt - 4);
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A smaller honest file loses money but protects trust and later audits.";
Q.news_headline = "The government submits a smaller independently audited KPO file";
!}

We claim less than we could and have the claim verified by auditors we do not
control. Money that might have been argued for is left on the table.

What is bought with it is the one thing a recovery programme cannot recover
once lost: a file that later scrutiny will confirm rather than unpick. The
Commission notices. So, eventually, will the next government.

- @kpo_result: Submit the honest file

@final_paper_close
title: Certify every arguable milestone and fight over it later
subtitle: Meet the filing date by transferring the crisis to auditors and courts.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 6;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 4;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 7;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure -= 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 5;
Q.public_trust -= 4;
Q.razem_dissent += 7;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change -= 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -4;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The filing deadline is met by transferring the crisis to audits and courts.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition certifies a contested final KPO file";
!}

Every arguable milestone is certified and the deadline is met. The claim goes
in complete, on time, and containing several statements that will need to be
defended.

The defending will be done by auditors, lawyers and whoever holds the ministry
in two years. We have converted a delivery problem into a legal one, which is
slower, quieter, and somebody else's.

- @kpo_result: Certify and defend later

@final_opposition_rescue
title: Support a narrow completion act for workers and municipalities
subtitle: Supply passage votes for useful projects and leave delivery ownership with the cabinet.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 3;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The Left supplies passage votes for useful projects without claiming to implement them from opposition.";
Q.news_headline = "Opposition votes rescue the final social KPO projects";
!}

We supply the votes for the completion act because municipal works and labour
projects are inside it. The government gets its majority and keeps every part
of the delivery it was always going to keep.

Our own side asks why we rescued a cabinet that will campaign against us in the
spring. The answer is the list of projects in the annex, which is a poor slogan
and a real one.

- @kpo_result: Pass the narrow act

@final_opposition_blame
title: Publish the missed-project map and refuse emergency cover
subtitle: Win the blame argument by mapping every project still exposed to the deadline.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.media_capacity += 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 6;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The map wins clear opposition credit while leaving weak projects exposed.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left maps every project endangered by the KPO deadline";
!}

The map goes out with every exposed project marked, dated and attributed to
the ministry responsible. No emergency cover, no rescue votes, no shared
ownership of a failure we did not cause.

It is the clearest political position available and it costs something real:
several of the projects on the map will now not be completed, and the towns
concerned can read their own names on it.

- @kpo_result: Publish the map


@kpo_result
title: The KPO ledger moves
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_delivery))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_public_credit =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_public_credit))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_public_credit)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_delayed =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
Q.kpo_progress_band =
    Q.kpo_delivery >= 24
        ? "Delivery visible"
        : (Q.kpo_delivery >= 12
            ? "Delivery partial"
            : "Delivery fragile");
!}

= The file moves

[+ kpo_last_summary +]

[? if kpo_delivery >= 24: In the counties, the fund has stopped being a word
from the news. There are sites with hoardings, contractors with signed dates
and clinics that have taken delivery of something. A programme people can walk
past is harder for any future minister to describe as somebody's abstraction.?]
[? if kpo_delivery >= 12 and kpo_delivery < 24: Enough has been signed to point
at, and not enough to answer the obvious question. Half the mayors on the list
have a start date; the other half have a letter explaining why theirs is
delayed, and every one of those letters is a small deposit of future anger.?]
[? if kpo_delivery < 12: On paper the plan is alive. On the ground almost
nothing has broken earth, and the people who were told to prepare bids are
beginning to treat the whole exercise as a Warsaw hobby.?]

[? if kpo_deadline_pressure >= 12: The 2026 completion date has stopped being a
horizon and become a problem. Every project office knows that work which cannot
finish cannot be certified, and that uncertified work is money returned.?]

[? if kpo_last_credit_change >= 4: **Our imprint is unmistakable.** Voters can
name what Lewica forced, and our partners can no longer fold it into a generic
government success.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change >= 1 and kpo_last_credit_change < 4:
**We have a claim, not ownership.** Our work is visible, but coalition partners
remain in the photograph and will contest the authorship.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change = 0: **The ledger moves without us.** The result
is administrative or belongs to the institution that acted.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change < 0: **We lose the story.** Work may continue, but
another party owns it or our factions inherit the blame.?]

[? if kpo_last_delivery_change >= 4: People, contracts and projects now move;
the advance is large enough to survive the press conference.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change >= 1 and kpo_last_delivery_change < 4:
Some implementation advances, but the next review can still expose what the
coalition left unfinished.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change = 0: We changed scrutiny or ownership, not what
the state can deliver.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change < 0: The paper file improved by displacing work
that people could have used.?]

[? if kpo_last_funds_change > 0: A further tranche has been released, still
subject to completion and audit.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
